{"step_index":196,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:27:47Z","content":"I have checked the available Model Context Protocol (MCP) integrations for **Draw.io** and **Excalidraw**, resolved an underlying npm cache permissions issue, and configured both MCP servers in your global Antigravity configuration.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Selected MCP Implementations\n\n| Tool | Package / Server | Description & Capabilities |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Draw.io** | [`@drawio/mcp`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@drawio/mcp) (v1.6.1) | **Official JGraph / Draw.io MCP server**.<br>• Generates and opens diagrams directly in the draw.io editor / browser.<br>• Supports XML (`open_drawio_xml`), CSV (`open_drawio_csv`), and Mermaid (`open_drawio_mermaid`).<br>• Includes `search_shapes` across 10,000+ shape libraries (AWS, Azure, GCP, Kubernetes, Cisco, UML, BPMN). |\n| **Excalidraw** | [`mcp-excalidraw-server`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/mcp-excalidraw-server) (v2.0) | **Full interactive canvas MCP server for coding agents**.<br>• Built specifically with support for Google Antigravity, Cursor, and Claude.<br>• Exposes 26 tools for element-level CRUD (create, update, delete, arrange, group, distribute).<br>• Supports Mermaid-to-Excalidraw conversion, live canvas inspection/screenshots, and exporting `.excalidraw` files to your workspace. |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Environment Fix & Validation\n\n* **npm Cache Permission Fix**: Fixed a cache collision in `~/.npm/_cacache` where legacy files owned by `nobody:nogroup` prevented npm/npx from completing package resolution. Recreated the cache under the current user (`koby`).\n* **Handshake Verification**: Verified the JSON-RPC stdio handshake on `@drawio/mcp`, confirming successful initialization (`serverInfo: { name: \"drawio-mcp\", version: \"1.6.1\" }`).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Configuration\n\nBoth servers have been added to your global configuration file in [~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json](file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"semaphore\": {\n      \"command\": \"/home/koby/.local/bin/semaphore-mcp\",\n      \"args\": [],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"SEMAPHORE_URL\": \"https://semaphore.corp.intranet.local\",\n        \"SEMAPHORE_API_TOKEN\": \"idjmlcr2-4355we8ydcffidc-cwd99k0cmo86v2zwju=\",\n        \"REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE\": \"/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt\",\n        \"SSL_CERT_FILE\": \"/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"drawio\": {\n      \"command\": \"/home/koby/.local/share/pi-node/current/bin/npx\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \"-y\",\n        \"@drawio/mcp\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"excalidraw\": {\n      \"command\": \"/home/koby/.local/share/pi-node/current/bin/npx\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \"-y\",\n        \"mcp-excalidraw-server\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Antigravity automatically initializes and discovers tools from configured MCP servers when starting a new session. To begin using the Draw.io and Excalidraw tools, restart your Antigravity session or reload your IDE window.","thinking":"The file read appears successful; the JSON structure is valid. Focusing on the JSON content now, looking for relevant configurations. The initial attempt to access a file in a specific directory was successful, confirming that the tool interaction is functioning as expected.\n\n\nFocusing on the configuration, it appears the system is set up to interact with both drawing and diagramming tools. Verification steps confirm the availability of a specific protocol implementation for one tool, including shape and diagram creation functionalities. Another diagramming solution's protocol implementation was also identified for interaction.\n\n\n"}
